1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,242
This is the CPI Assistant:

2
00:00:02,242 --> 00:00:07,118
an agent for SAP Cloud Integration, built like a small Claude Code.

3
00:00:07,118 --> 00:00:11,631
One question field, answers from SAP's official documentation,

4
00:00:11,631 --> 00:00:15,023
and tools when a question needs them.

5
00:00:15,483 --> 00:00:17,696
Every question takes one path.

6
00:00:17,696 --> 00:00:23,891
First, code finds the two best of 1,660 official SAP pages, by meaning and keywords,

7
00:00:23,891 --> 00:00:25,513
and saves them if new.

8
00:00:25,513 --> 00:00:30,085
Then the agent answers, calling tools only when it needs more.

9
00:00:30,085 --> 00:00:33,293
Finally every citation is checked.

10
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:38,540
com, under a Creative Commons licence.

11
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:48,317
The catalog is pinned to one commit, and nothing else can be downloaded.

12
00:00:48,783 --> 00:00:52,081
Live. A question the database cannot answer yet:

13
00:00:52,081 --> 00:00:57,576
the AS4 receiver adapter. The two best pages were downloaded from SAP and saved.

14
00:00:57,576 --> 00:01:02,603
The passages were enough, so the agent answered without a tool.

15
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:07,011
The same question again. Now both pages say: already saved.

16
00:01:07,011 --> 00:01:12,637
Nothing is downloaded; the passages come straight from the local database.

17
00:01:13,117 --> 00:01:15,120
Every answer lists its sources:

18
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:19,190
each page, how close its passage was, and whether it was cited.

19
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:22,862
A page cited but never given would be flagged.

20
00:01:23,317 --> 00:01:25,959
Each source links to where it came from:

21
00:01:25,959 --> 00:01:29,263
here, that page in SAP's documentation repository.

22
00:01:29,263 --> 00:01:32,870
The official text the answer was built from.

23
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:38,182
When the passages are not enough, the agent has a kit, like Claude Code:

24
00:01:38,182 --> 00:01:43,450
tools to read a whole page or search more, skills with step-by-step playbooks,

25
00:01:43,450 --> 00:01:46,649
the live CPI tenant, and MCP servers.

26
00:01:47,099 --> 00:01:49,788
A tenant question: why did Order_Sync fail?

27
00:01:49,788 --> 00:01:53,039
The agent calls the tenant tools one step at a time:

28
00:01:53,039 --> 00:01:56,479
the problem messages, then the error of the newest one,

29
00:01:56,479 --> 00:01:59,617
and answers with the cause and the fix.

30
00:02:00,099 --> 00:02:03,879
Every tool call is shown with its arguments and its full result,

31
00:02:03,879 --> 00:02:07,177
so you can check exactly what the agent saw.

32
00:02:07,632 --> 00:02:09,443
Which iFlows are not running?

33
00:02:09,443 --> 00:02:14,567
Here the agent first loads a skill, check tenant health, and follows its playbook:

34
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:17,953
list the iFlows, then the problem messages.

35
00:02:18,432 --> 00:02:21,026
A question outside Cloud Integration:

36
00:02:21,026 --> 00:02:25,373
no SAP page matches, nothing is downloaded, no tool is called,

37
00:02:25,373 --> 00:02:29,158
and the agent declines instead of inventing.

38
00:02:29,632 --> 00:02:34,220
Every tool call, ours or an MCP server's, passes the same hooks:

39
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:39,741
arguments are checked before, results limited after, and each call is logged.

40
00:02:39,741 --> 00:02:46,033
MCP servers expose only allowlisted tools, and the tenant tools are read-only.

41
00:02:46,498 --> 00:02:50,378
Locally we keep SAP's text only, never a model's answer:

42
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:53,704
chunks with the page title, link and fetch time.

43
00:02:53,704 --> 00:02:58,000
A page older than 30 days is downloaded again on its next use,

44
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:03,412
and the catalog is rebuilt from SAP's latest commit with one script.

45
00:03:03,865 --> 00:03:07,648
Measured on fifteen documentation questions, some reworded,

46
00:03:07,648 --> 00:03:13,163
against a model that searches the files itself; and fourteen checks on the live agent.

47
00:03:13,163 --> 00:03:15,530
The results are on screen.

48
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:20,423
The model runs locally, or on OpenAI or Claude with one setting.

49
00:03:20,423 --> 00:03:25,704
This narration is a synthetic voice, generated locally. Thank you.
